### Natural radioactivity of the steel plate of macro/beam_steel_lyso.mac, one job (2026-11-10, the steel study with
### U, Th and K impurities; condor/beam_steel_submit.sh writes and submits the jobs, band decay). The same setup: the
### 20 x 20 x 1 cm plate at 32.5-33.5 cm on the pixel panel bmPanel (macro/panel_<bmPanel>.mac, centre at bmPanelZ cm).
### Each event is one nucleus bmIonZ, bmIonA at rest, placed uniformly in the plate, that decays with its whole chain in
### the same event: Geant4 skips the decay of nuclides that live longer than 1 year (U-238, U-234, Th-230, Ra-226,
### Pb-210, Th-232, Ra-228, Th-228, K-40, ...) unless that threshold is raised, as here. One event is then one decay of
### every member of the chain, as in secular equilibrium (each member as active as the parent); the members' decays lie
### up to 10^17 s apart, so each gives hits of its own (the panel's hits group deposits within 100 ns). The analysis
### (analysis/beam_steel_trace_spectrum.C) scales the events to the activity of the impurity in the plate.
### Only events with energy in the panel are written (/EventFilter 7); the number of decays is the run tree's n_events.
### The job macro sets the aliases bmSeed, bmEvents, bmDir, bmFile, bmPanel, bmPanelZ, bmIonZ and bmIonA, the target's
### /tof/target/composition and density (the plate's own absorption), then executes this. Needs TOFmeter --preinit
### macro/preinit_lyso.mac (radioactive decay and fluorescence; nothing of the LYSO).
/tof/det/worldSize 420 420 300 cm
/tof/det/stack false
/tof/target/size 20 20 1 cm
/tof/target/position 0 0 33.0 cm
/control/execute macro/panel_{bmPanel}.mac
/tof/czt/position 0 0 {bmPanelZ} cm
/update
/OutputFormat 1
/EventFilter 7
/OutputDirectory {bmDir}
/OutputFile {bmFile}
/gun/seed {bmSeed}
/GeneralParticleSource 1
/gps/particle ion
/gps/ion {bmIonZ} {bmIonA} 0 0
/gps/pos/type Volume
/gps/pos/shape Para
/gps/pos/centre 0 0 33.0 cm
/gps/pos/halfx 10 cm
/gps/pos/halfy 10 cm
/gps/pos/halfz 0.5 cm
/gps/pos/confine Target
/gps/ang/type iso
/gps/ene/type Mono
/gps/ene/mono 0 keV
/process/had/rdm/thresholdForVeryLongDecayTime 1.0e+60 year
# Auger electrons off (their few keV stay where they are made), as in the beam jobs; fluorescence stays on
/process/em/auger false
/process/em/augerCascade false
# verbose 1: the log ends with "Number of events processed : <bmEvents>", which the job script looks for
/run/verbose 1
/run/printProgress 100000
/run/beamOn {bmEvents}
